# ============================================================
# Diceman175 Workspace - Git Ignore (canonical source)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Real file lives at:
#   governator175/symlink-target/root-files/.gitignore
# Distributed as a real committed copy into every repo root, and as a real
# (non-committed) copy at the workspace root, by
# governator175/symlink-target/scripts/rules/a12-git-attributes/sync-git-infrastructure.ps1
#
# This is the REPO-COMMITTED baseline every clone, collaborator, and CI run
# sees. It is distinct from two other .gitignore-adjacent files that stay
# out of A12's scope on purpose:
#   - symlink-target/github/config/gitignore   - machine-local core.excludesFile;
#     applies only on this machine, never committed, never seen by a clone.
#   - symlink-target/templates/git/template-gitignore - a fill-in-the-blanks
#     starter for brand-new repos (has {{placeholders}}), not synced content.
#
# EVIDENCE BASE (2026-08-10): built from a pattern-frequency analysis of the
# 20 existing per-repo .gitignore files already in the workspace (see
# TEMP/a12-git-infrastructure/gitignore-pattern-frequency-analysis.csv).
# The governance-symlink, .claude/.vscode, and secrets blocks are copied
# verbatim from the two most current hand-maintained files (Neural-Net and
# governator175's own .gitignore). The Node.js/Python blocks are the near-
# complete union of what 5 of the 20 repos (Scripts, epub2Audiobook, mjpb,
# My-Jira-Prompt-Builder, My-Research-and-Action-Hub) already carry verbatim
# from the standard gitignore.io templates - folded in wholesale on
# 2026-08-10 after a real coverage check showed the first (trimmed) version
# of this file would have dropped real, in-use patterns from those repos.
#
# DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED as repo-specific, not master material (checked
# against real per-repo content, not guessed):
#   - Named-project paths/negations: rag-corpus-tools/*, !rag-corpus-tools/...,
#     scripts/sync.log, _session-logs/ (MTBank); mlx-env/ (repo-specific venv name)
#   - governator175-internal runtime paths: governator/logs/, audit/reports/*.csv,
#     endoskeleton/claude-code/.claude/audit/, symlink-target/scripts/.../logs/
#   - Neural-Net's own /plans/ (repo-root path specific to how that repo lays
#     out planning docs - NOT the same as project-genisys/01-cyberdyne-concepts/,
#     which is the actual tracked plans tree and must never be ignored)
#   - /pgdata/, /server/exports/, /*.png (single-repo, narrow purpose)
#   - *.mp3 - would actively break epub2Audiobook, which intentionally commits
#     audio fixtures/output
#
# Known limitation: like .gitattributes/.editorconfig/.markdownlint.json,
# this file must be byte-identical across every repo to pass -Mode Check.
# A repo needing a genuinely one-off ignore rule outside the categories
# above will show as permanent drift - accepted, same tension already
# exists for the other three A12-governed files.
# ============================================================

