# Sidecar settings files (*.settings.jsonc) - DECISION (2026-09-05): several
# tools write their own current settings back to a <tool-name>.settings.jsonc
# sidecar next to themselves at runtime (e.g. a "PersistSettings"/"persist
# settings" flag), so the file on disk is regenerated from whatever the last
# invocation's flags/UI state were, not hand-authored. Untracked going
# forward so a fresh sidecar (like confluence-image-factory's, discovered
# never committed) doesn't show up as noise to add by accident.
# NOTE: gitignore never untracks a file already committed (git does not
# retroactively stop tracking a tracked path via .gitignore). Several tools
# in Neural-Net (universal-archive-backup-validator, f5scope, view-csv-
# interactive, git-safe-move-*, repo-clones-*, and others) intentionally
# commit their .settings.jsonc as versioned state and keep doing so -
# this rule only affects settings sidecars that aren't tracked yet.
*.settings.jsonc
